      "side": 1,
      "message": "Hi,\n\nCompressedBitmap.iterator() can yield the same OID twice during a\nbitmap walk with index misses: once from the mutableIndex range and\nonce from the ofObjectType range. PackWriter.addObject() does not\ndeduplicate, so the object is written to the pack twice.\n\nThe client rejects it with:\n  fatal: The same object \u003coid\u003e appears twice in the pack\n\nWe hit this in production on repos with low bitmap coverage (e.g. old\nrepos where only ~11% of commits have precomputed bitmaps) and midx\nenabled. It is 100% reproducible, not a race condition.\n\nFix: use addIfAbsent() in addObject() — one line change, no\nallocation overhead.",
      "revId": "f4ba16dfa85fee11361e82afdcc7fdf347513f4a",
      "serverId": "d5d70762-12d0-45a1-890d-524b12d3f735"
    },
